[{"data":1,"prerenderedAt":116},["ShallowReactive",2],{"content-term":3,"content-events-lt-02-human-rights":10,"content-footer":43,"content-navLinks":83,"content-socialLinks":97},{"id":4,"extension":5,"meta":6,"stem":7,"term":8,"__hash__":9},"term\u002Fterm.yaml","yaml",{},"term","Summer Term 2021","SQOHq2z20YBZmK3Tbszg4OjlJQoD3LZuHGVnvNUzSUw",{"id":11,"title":12,"date":13,"description":14,"extension":5,"forms":15,"is_public":21,"meetings":22,"meta":28,"resources":29,"showResources":21,"stem":40,"__hash__":41,"slug":42},"events\u002Fevents\u002Flt-02-human-rights.yaml","Lightning Talk #2: Human Rights & Design Thinking","2021-05-11T19:30:00+02:00","In this talk, __Charlotte Seiler__ and __Vanessa Giersdorf__ ([Getting There Consulting](https:\u002F\u002Fwww.gettingthere-consulting.com\u002F)) will introduce their Human Rights-Centered Design approach and apply this to the subject of AI.\n\nAs Artificial Intelligence evolves, so do the many controversies that surround the use of this advanced technology. It is therefore crucial to understand its impact on a societal and public policy level. Scenarios in problem areas: privacy, explainability, reliability and risks of complex systems, responsibility of professionals for applications and consequences of their work.\n\nCharlotte and Vanessa believe that data science and machine learning can help us design intelligent products, services, and systems that improve people’s everyday lives. But in order to have a truly positive impact, AI-powered technologies must be grounded in human rights and work to extend and enhance our capabilities, not replace them.\n",[16],{"title":17,"type":18,"description":19,"url":20},"Feedback: Lightning Talk #2","form","Please leave your feedback!","https:\u002F\u002Ftechlabsorg.typeform.com\u002Fto\u002FU67ml5lG",true,[23],{"title":24,"description":25,"type":26,"url":27},"Meet: Lightning Talk #2","The main room where we will meet.","meeting","https:\u002F\u002Fus02web.zoom.us\u002Fj\u002F82570